<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Opening in VS Code (Windows + WSL)</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Open VS Code on Windows</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Press <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Ctrl+Shift+P</code> → type <strong>"WSL: Open Folder in WSL"</strong> → select your project folder at <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/home/manoj/ai-credit-card-fraud-detection</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Once open, use <strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Ctrl+`` </code></strong> to open the integrated terminal — it will be a WSL terminal</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Split into 2 terminals (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">+</code> button) and run backend in one, frontend in the other</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Make sure you have the <strong>WSL extension</strong> installed in VS Code (search "WSL" in Extensions panel).</p>
