<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 2 — Install WSL Extension (One-time, Important)</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Press <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Ctrl+Shift+X</code> to open Extensions</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Search <strong>"WSL"</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Install the one by <strong>Microsoft</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">After installing, press <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Ctrl+Shift+P</code> → type <strong>"Reopen in WSL"</strong> → press Enter</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Your VS Code title bar will now show <strong>[WSL: Ubuntu]</strong> — this means your terminal is now a real Linux terminal, not Windows CMD.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 3 — Open 2 Terminals Side by Side</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Press <strong>Ctrl+`</strong> to open the terminal panel.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Then click the <strong>"+"</strong> icon (or <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Ctrl+Shift+5</code>) to split into two terminals.</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Left terminal</strong> → Backend</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Right terminal</strong> → Frontend</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
