me explain clearly.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Why WSL Was Needed Before</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">When you originally built this project, you used <strong>WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux)</strong> because:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">The project runs on <strong>Python + FastAPI + Node.js</strong> which work best on Linux</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">All your project files are <strong>stored inside WSL's Linux filesystem</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Commands like <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">source venv/bin/activate</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">npm run dev</code> are <strong>Linux commands</strong></li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">So your entire project (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fraud-backend</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fraud-frontend</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fraud-ml</code>) is sitting <strong>inside WSL's disk</strong>, not on your Windows C: or D: drive.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">But Here's the Good News</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">You have <strong>two options</strong> to run this project. WSL is just one of them.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class="min-w-full border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal"><thead class="text-left"><tr><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Option</th><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top"><strong>WSL</strong></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Your original setup, project files in Linux</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top"><strong>Rebuild on Windows</strong></td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Recreate the project directly on D: drive, no WSL needed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">My Honest Recommendation</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Since your C: drive is <strong>completely full</strong> and WSL is broken, the <strong>fastest path</strong> is:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Rebuild the project directly on Windows (D: drive)</strong> using:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Python for Windows</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Node.js for Windows</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">VS Code on Windows</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">No WSL needed at all. Everything runs natively.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
