<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This folder stores everything the ML model learned. Think of it as saving a trained doctor's knowledge into files so you can use it anytime without retraining.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fraud_model.pkl</code> — The Trained ML Brain</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.pkl</code> means "pickle" — Python's way of saving any object to a file</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Contains the entire Gradient Boosting model after training</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">File size is typically 5-50 MB</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">When loaded, it can instantly score any transaction</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Analogy:</strong> Imagine training a fraud expert for 2 minutes (training time) and then freezing their brain into a file. Later you wake them up in milliseconds to check any transaction.</p>
