-</span><span>no-cache-</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 81, 194);">dir</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">--no-cache-dir</code> forces pip to skip C: drive cache entirely.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Actually — We Don't Need Locust</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Since C: drive keeps blocking installations, let's <strong>skip Locust</strong> and use Python's built-in <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">threading</code> to do load testing instead.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">It gives the same results — real throughput numbers — with zero extra installation.</p>
