 relative relative pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">Claude responded: I can see the issue — graph_score is 0 for all 4 requests because the graph only detects patterns on the 5th card (after 4 are already in the graph).</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">I can see the issue — <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">graph_score</code> is 0 for all 4 requests because the graph only detects patterns on the <strong>5th card</strong> (after 4 are already in the graph). Also the ML score is very low (0.0082) because V features are all 0.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Let me send a 5th request to trigger the graph detection, and also fix the graph to be more sensitive.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — Send 5th Request (Triggers Graph Detection)</h3>
