<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What Google SDE 1 Interview Actually Tests</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Google SDE 1 has 4-5 rounds:</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class="min-w-full border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal"><thead class="text-left"><tr><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Round</th><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">What they test</th><th scope="col" class="text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Your readiness</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Coding round 1</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">DSA — arrays, strings, trees</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Depends on LeetCode prep</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Coding round 2</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">DSA — graphs, DP</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Depends on LeetCode prep</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">System design (light)</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Design a simple system</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">✅ Very strong</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Behavioral</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Leadership, impact, ownership</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">✅ Strong project story</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Project deep dive</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">Explain what you built</td><td class="border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.3)] py-2 pr-4 align-top">✅ Extremely strong</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Your Strongest Cards</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>1. Project depth</strong> — Most SDE 1 candidates have tutorial projects. You have a system with chaos testing, Redis pipelines, graph detection, and load test results. That's rare.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>2. System design</strong> — You can draw and explain a multi-layer architecture with real trade-offs. Most new grads can't.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>3. Numbers</strong> — You have real metrics: 18,327 req/min, P95 47ms, ROC-AUC 0.9850, zero errors at 100 threads. Interviewers love specific numbers.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>4. Failure handling</strong> — You know what happens when Redis dies. Most candidates never think about this.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Your Weakest Area (Be Honest)</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>DSA / LeetCode</strong> — Google SDE 1 is primarily a coding interview. Your project is impressive but won't replace DSA.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">If you haven't done consistent LeetCode practice, that's where you need to focus alongside this project.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
