<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 3 — Create a Streamlit-Compatible Dashboard</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The current <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">dashboard.py</code> calls <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">http://127.0.0.1:8000</code> (your local FastAPI). On Streamlit Cloud there's no FastAPI running — so we need a standalone version that calls the ML model directly without needing the backend.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Run these first then I'll give you the new dashboard file:</p>
