span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(179, 74, 0);">str</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span>uuid</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">.</span><span>uuid4</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">)</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">)</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">[</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">:</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">8</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">]</span><span>  </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># "7d9631dc"</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Every request gets a unique 8-character ID the moment it arrives. This ID appears in every log line for that request. If a customer calls and says "my transaction was blocked", you search for their request ID and instantly find every log line related to that specific transaction.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This is called <strong>distributed tracing</strong> — a key concept in production systems.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The /health Endpoint</h3>
