<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Who uses /health?</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Load balancers ping it every 30 seconds</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Kubernetes uses it for automatic restarts</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">On-call engineers check it first when something breaks</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Monitoring systems alert if it stops returning "ok"</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Interview Answer for Phase 5</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"I implemented structured JSON logging with unique request IDs for every transaction. This enables distributed tracing — if something goes wrong, I can search logs by request ID and reconstruct exactly what happened. I also built /health and /metrics endpoints that expose system state including uptime, Redis status, fraud rates, and approval rates. In production, these feed into monitoring dashboards."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">⚡ Phase 6 — Load Testing</h2>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Why Load Test?</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-pre-wrap">"My system works for 1 user" is not enough.
"My system handles 18,327 requests per minute with zero errors" is a real metric.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Load testing answers:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">How many requests per minute can we handle?</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">At what concurrency does latency degrade?</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Does the system break under extreme load?</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">What's the P95 latency? (95% of users experience this or better)</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What P95 Latency Means</h3>
<div role="group" aria-label="Code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
