</span><span>  Redis restart → automatic reconnection → state preserved
</span><span>  No manual intervention needed
</span><span>
</span><span>Zero errors: ✅
</span><span>  No 500 errors, no crashes, no data loss
</span><span>  System self-heals</span></code></pre></div></div>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Interview Answer for Phase 7</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"I chaos tested the system by killing Redis mid-traffic. The system automatically detected Redis unavailability and switched to in-memory rate limiting with zero downtime — all requests continued returning 200. When Redis was restored, the system automatically reconnected and preserved the rate limit state. This proves production resilience without manual intervention."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
