</span><span>  Fraud Detected    → how many blocked
</span><span>  Fraud Rate %      → what % of traffic is fraud
</span><span>  Graph Nodes       → how big the graph is
</span><span>
</span><span>Load test results:  → static table showing proven performance
</span><span>Chaos test results: → showing ✅ PASSED
</span><span>Model performance:  → ROC-AUC, Recall, etc.</span></code></pre></div></div>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Interview Answer for Phase 8</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"I built a 3-tab Streamlit dashboard entirely in Python. Tab 1 lets you score individual transactions and see ML score, graph score, and explanation side by side. Tab 2 demonstrates fraud ring detection — you simulate multiple cards through the same merchant and IP, and watch the graph risk score escalate in real time as the ring builds. Tab 3 shows live system metrics and the proven load test results. The dashboard is deployed on Streamlit Cloud for live demo access."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">🚀 Phase 9 — GitHub + Deployment</h2>
