</span></span><span>Merchant:    Amazon India
</span><span>Location:    Bangalore
</span><span>Amount:      ₹2,500
</span><span>Time:        2:15 AM</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Problem:</strong> You cannot share this data. It contains:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Customer card numbers (private)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Merchant names (business sensitive)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Customer locations (privacy law violation)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Transaction patterns (can identify individuals)</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">In India this violates RBI guidelines. In Europe it violates GDPR. Banks can be fined crores for sharing this.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What Is PCA?</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">PCA stands for <strong>Principal Component Analysis</strong>. It's a mathematical technique that:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Takes your original data (28 columns of real bank features)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Mixes them together mathematically</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Creates new columns (V1-V28) that contain the same information</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">But are impossible to reverse-engineer back to original data</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Simple analogy:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Imagine you have a recipe:</p>
