<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">They don't know what V14 means in real terms either. They just know "when V14 is very negative, it correlates strongly with fraud." That's enough.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Interview Answer</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"V1-V28 are PCA-transformed features. Banks can't share raw transaction data — card numbers, merchant names, locations — due to privacy laws. PCA mathematically transforms the original 28 features into new ones that preserve fraud patterns but make it impossible to recover personal information. Real fraud engineers at Visa and Mastercard work with these exact anonymized features. Our model learned that V14 is the strongest fraud predictor with 72% feature importance — it captures some combination of original fraud signals that we don't need to understand explicitly."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
