tBoostingClassifier</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    n_estimators</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">200</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>     </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># 200 trees</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    learning_rate</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">0.05</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>   </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># each tree contributes 5% </span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    max_depth</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">4</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>          </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># each tree can ask 4 questions max</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    min_samples_leaf</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">20</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>  </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># each leaf needs 20+ samples</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    random_state</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">42</span><span>       </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(110, 118, 135);"># reproducible results</span><span>
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">)</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>n_estimators=200:</strong>
More trees = more accurate but slower. 200 is a good balance. At 500 trees accuracy barely improves but training takes 2.5x longer.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>learning_rate=0.05:</strong>
Small learning rate = each tree contributes a little = less overfitting. Large learning rate = each tree contributes a lot = overfits. 0.05 is industry standard.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>max_depth=4:</strong>
Limits how complex each individual tree can be. Prevents overfitting. Each tree can only ask 4 levels of yes/no questions.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>min_samples_leaf=20:</strong>
Each final decision node must have at least 20 training examples. Prevents the model from making rules based on too few examples.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">📊 Results — Complete Explanation With Examples</h2>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">ROC-AUC = 0.9850</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>What ROC-AUC actually means — step by step:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Imagine you have a bag with 75 fraud transactions and 56,887 normal transactions.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-pre-wrap">You randomly pick 1 fraud and 1 normal transaction.
You show both to the model.
The model gives each a risk score.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Question: Does the model rank the fraud higher than the normal?</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">ROC-AUC 0.9850 means: <strong>YES, 98.5% of the time.</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Real example:</strong></p>
<div role="group" aria-label="Code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
