</span></span><span>Accuracy of our model = 99.29%
</span><span>
</span><span>Our model looks WORSE by accuracy!
</span><span>But our model catches 64 frauds. The naive model catches 0.
</span><span>
</span><span>Accuracy is useless for imbalanced data.
</span><span>ROC-AUC measures ranking quality, not raw accuracy.</span></code></pre></div></div>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Recall = 85.33%</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>What recall means:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Out of all the actual fraud cases, what percentage did we catch?</p>
