<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Only specific trusted origins allowed. This prevents external attackers from calling your API from their websites.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">📚 Swagger Documentation — Complete Explanation</h2>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What Is Swagger?</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Swagger (now called OpenAPI) is an industry standard for documenting APIs. It creates a web page where developers can:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">See all available endpoints</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">See what data each endpoint accepts</li>
