<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Why Risk Score Shows 0.0000</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The test transaction uses <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">V1-V28 = 0.0</code> (all zeros). LightGBM learned that zero V-features = normal transaction. The V-features carry 80%+ of the fraud signal. The velocity/amount features alone aren't enough to trigger a high score without the V-features matching fraud patterns.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This is actually correct behavior — it means the model isn't fooled by just high amounts or night time alone. It needs the actual bank signal patterns (V features) to confirm fraud.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
