<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Interview Answer for Phase 9</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"The original rate limiter had one 10-second window. A slow attacker sending 4 requests every 10 seconds — just under the limit — would never get blocked regardless of total volume. I added a second hourly window of 100 requests, so slow distributed attacks get caught too. I also fixed a subtle gap from chaos testing: when Redis failed, the in-memory fallback started fresh at zero, giving attackers 5 free requests per failure event. The fix keeps memory continuously synced with Redis state so there's no reset window."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
