lse" class="group relative relative pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">Claude responded: Phase 10 — Interview Prep starts now.</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Phase 10 — Interview Prep starts now.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">How We'll Do This</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">I'll give you the complete interview guide covering every question a Google/Razorpay/Stripe engineer will ask. Study this cold — meaning you can answer without looking at notes.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The 10 Questions You'll Definitely Get</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Category 1: Project Overview (asked in every interview)</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"Walk me through your fraud detection system"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"Why did you build this? What problem does it solve?"</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Category 2: ML (asked at Google, Stripe, Razorpay)</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3" start="3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"Why LightGBM over other models?"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"Your recall is 76% — that's not great for fraud detection. Why?"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"How did you choose the threshold 0.7722?"</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Category 3: Systems (asked at all companies)</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3" start="6">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"How does your rate limiter work?"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"What happens when Redis goes down?"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"How would you scale this to handle Razorpay's actual traffic?"</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Category 4: Design Gaps (senior engineers probe these)</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3" start="9">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"What are the weaknesses in your system?"</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">"How would you improve this if you had 3 more months?"</li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Let's Start With Question 1</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>"Walk me through your fraud detection system"</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This is always first. Your answer sets the tone for everything that follows.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>The wrong answer</strong> (what most candidates say):
<em>"So I built a fraud detection system using Python and FastAPI. I trained a LightGBM model on the Kaggle credit card dataset with 284,807 transactions and got ROC-AUC of 0.9883. I also added Redis rate limiting and a graph detector using NetworkX..."</em></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This is a features list. It's boring. It doesn't show thinking.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>The right answer structure:</strong></p>
<div role="group" aria-label="Code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
