</span></span><span>2. Architecture overview (2 sentences)
</span><span>3. The interesting technical decision (2 sentences)
</span><span>4. Results (1 sentence)
</span><span>5. Stop talking</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Here's your exact answer:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"Credit card fraud costs banks billions annually — the challenge is catching fraud without blocking legitimate customers. I built a 4-layer system: a dual-window Redis rate limiter stops card-testing attacks before ML runs, a LightGBM model scores transaction risk, a graph detector catches fraud rings by tracking card-merchant-IP relationships in real time, and structured JSON logging gives full observability. The interesting decision was the threshold — pure cost optimization suggested 0.02, but with a 90% precision constraint to protect customer experience, the optimal threshold became 0.7722, saving ₹1,800 per test window vs the default. Live at 16,215 req/min with zero errors under 100-thread load."</em></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>That's 90 seconds. Stop there.</strong></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Now Practice This Out Loud</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Say it out loud right now — not in your head, out loud. Time yourself.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Then come back and tell me:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">How long did it take?</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Which part felt awkward?</li>
