</span></span><span>Value: sorted set of timestamps
</span><span>
</span><span>On each request:
</span><span>1. Remove timestamps older than 10 seconds
</span><span>2. Count remaining (requests in last 10s)
</span><span>3. If count &gt;= 5 → BLOCK (429)
</span><span>4. Add current timestamp
</span><span>5. Set key expiry
</span><span>All 4 steps in one atomic Redis pipeline</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Why Redis over in-memory?</strong> With 8 uvicorn workers, each worker has its own memory. Without Redis:</p>
