</span></span><span>Worker 2: User has 0 requests → 5 more allowed!
</span><span>= Attacker gets 40 requests across 8 workers</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Redis is shared across all workers — everyone sees the same counter.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Graceful degradation:</strong> Redis down → automatic fallback to in-memory → zero downtime. This was proven in chaos testing.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">📝 Phase 4 — Structured Logging + Observability</h2>
