</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">}</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Why JSON?</strong> Machine readable. Can feed into Elasticsearch, Splunk, CloudWatch. Plain text can't be searched or filtered programmatically.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Why request_id?</strong> If a customer calls saying "my transaction was blocked," you search by request_id and find every log line related to that exact transaction in milliseconds. This is called <strong>distributed tracing</strong>.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">New endpoints: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/health</code> (system status), <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/metrics</code> (fraud rates).</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">🕸️ Phase 5 — Graph-Based Fraud Ring Detection</h2>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>The problem ML can't solve:</strong></p>
<div role="group" aria-label="Code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
