</span></span><span>FP      : 4 (was 395 — 98.9% reduction!)
</span><span>Recall  : 76% (was 85.33% — tradeoff accepted)
</span><span>Training: 12.5s</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>The tradeoff decision:</strong> 395 false positives means blocking 395 legitimate customers per test window. That's unacceptable for customer experience. We consciously traded 9% recall for a 98.9% reduction in false alarms.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>SMOTE was tried and rejected:</strong> SMOTE created 22,325 synthetic fraud examples but actually dropped ROC-AUC to 0.9732 with the same 76% recall. The 18 missed frauds score below 0.30 regardless — they're genuinely ambiguous transactions with no distinguishing signal.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.375rem] font-bold">💰 Phase 8 — Threshold Optimization</h2>
