<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The honest interview answer is now even stronger:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"I tried 5 different LightGBM configurations — varying num_leaves from 31 to 255, scale_pos_weight from 545 to 2180, and min_child_samples from 3 to 20. All configurations converged to 76% recall with 18 missed frauds. Investigation confirmed these 18 transactions score below 0.30 regardless of configuration — they're genuinely indistinguishable from normal transactions in the V1-V28 feature space. This is a dataset limitation, not a modeling limitation."</em></p>
