 pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">Claude responded: Docker daemon is not running.</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Docker daemon is not running. You need to start Docker Desktop first.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Start Docker Desktop</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Look for Docker Desktop in your taskbar or Start menu:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Press <strong>Windows key</strong> and search <strong>"Docker Desktop"</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click to open it</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Wait for it to start — you'll see the Docker whale icon in the system tray turn from spinning to solid</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">It takes about 1-2 minutes to fully start</li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
