<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What V1-V28 Actually Are</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Remember — V1-V28 are <strong>PCA-transformed bank features</strong>. They encode:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Merchant category (grocery vs electronics vs ATM)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Transaction history patterns</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Device fingerprint</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Location history</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Spending behavior</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The bank's transaction processing pipeline generates these automatically for every real transaction.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>In our demo, we have no bank pipeline — so V-features default to 0.</strong></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
