<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The bank anonymized everything via PCA. Geographic data was stripped.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What This Means for Interviews</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Be honest about this:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"The geographic risk module uses country risk levels and impossible travel detection. In production, the bank's transaction processor provides country and city metadata with each transaction. Our Kaggle dataset is fully anonymized — no geographic data available — so we validated the logic with synthetic test cases covering high-risk countries, VPN detection, and impossible travel scenarios."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Is This Still Interview-Worthy?</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Yes — for two reasons:</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">The logic is correct and production-realistic. Real fraud systems at Visa/Razorpay use exactly these signals.</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">You understand the limitation — which is more impressive than pretending it works on real data.</li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Want to Validate It Properly?</h3>
