<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">process_batch</code> function calls <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">rate_limiter.is_allowed(client_ip, "batch")</code> which hits the regular 5/10s limit.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">The fix — pass <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">None</code> as rate_limiter to use only the batch-specific limits:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Change to:</p>
