ss="token token decorator annotation" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">.</span><span class="token token decorator annotation" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">post</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 0);">"/fraud/check/batch"</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">)</span><span>
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(129, 0, 194);">async</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(129, 0, 194);">def</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 81, 194);">check_fraud_batch</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span>batch</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">:</span><span> BatchRequest</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span> request</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">:</span><span> Request</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">)</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">:</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>    </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(129, 0, 194);">return</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(129, 0, 194);">await</span><span> process_batch</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">(</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>        batch        </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span> batch</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>        client_ip    </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span> request</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">.</span><span>client</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">.</span><span>host</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>        rate_limiter </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(20, 24, 31);">=</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(0, 128, 128);">None</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(43, 48, 59);">,</span><span>  ← this</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>The reason:</strong> The batch endpoint has its own dedicated rate limiter inside <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">batch_processor.py</code> with higher limits (500/10s instead of 5/10s). Passing <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">None</code> tells <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">process_batch</code> to skip the regular per-IP rate limiter and use only the batch-specific one.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Is this correct?</strong> Yes — batch requests come from trusted internal services (bank's batch processor), not end users. They need higher throughput limits.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Could we do better?</strong> Yes — pass the actual rate_limiter and let <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">process_batch</code> use <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">_check_batch_rate_limit</code> internally. But <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">None</code> works correctly for now.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Now Build Redis-Backed Shared Graph</h3></div></div><div class="mt-4"><div class="grid grid-rows-[auto_auto] min-w-0"><div class="row-start-1 col-start-1 min-w-0"><div class="min-w-0 pl-2 py-1.5"><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><button class="group/status flex items-center gap-2 py-1 text-sm transition-colors cursor-pointer text-left text-text-500 hover:text-text-300 flex-1 min-w-0" aria-expanded="false"><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 min-w-0" style="opacity: 1;"><span class="truncate font-base">Ran a command, read a file</span><span class="inline-flex transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 -rotate-90"><div style="width: 12px; height: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" style="flex-shrink: 0;"><path d="M14.128 7.165a.502.502 0 0 1 .744.67l-4.5 5-.078.07a.5.5 0 0 1-.666-.07l-4.5-5-.06-.082a.501.501 0 0 1 .729-.656l.075.068L10 11.752z"></path></svg></div></span></div></button></div><span class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ran a command, read a file</span><div class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-300 ease-out" style="grid-template-rows: 0fr;"><div class="overflow-hidden min-w-0"></div></div></div></div><div class="row-start-2 col-start-1 relative grid isolate min-w-0"><div class="row-start-1 col-start-1 relative z-[2] min-w-0"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Save to <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">D:\fraud-detection\redis_graph.py</code> then run:</p>
