<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">This is because Redis graph adds overhead per request. The sync endpoint now does Redis lookups for EVERY transaction. The async endpoints are fine (13ms, 214ms).</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">For interview purposes this is actually a good story:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><em>"Adding Redis-backed shared graph increased sync endpoint P95 from 24ms to 1646ms — each request now makes 4 Redis round trips for graph lookups. The fix is the async endpoint which returns in 13ms P95 by doing graph lookups in the background. This is why async architecture matters at scale."</em></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
