<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Problem First</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">FraudShield AI calls your fraud API at <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">localhost:8000</code> — but Streamlit Cloud can't reach your laptop's localhost.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Solution:</strong> Make the agent work standalone without needing the local API running. We add a <strong>demo mode</strong> that simulates the fraud API responses.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — Add Demo Mode to Detection Agent</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Open <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">D:\fraudshield-agent\agents\detection_agent.py</code></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Add this at the top of <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">check_transaction</code> method, right after <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">self.total_calls += 1</code>:</p>
